    {
      "id": "get-vertex",
      "name": "GetVertex",
      "category": "AABB",
      "signature": "GetVertex(Target, Index)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TAABB*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Index",
          "type": "Int"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TVector<T,d>",
      "docs": "Get a vector one of the eight corners of the box.\nEach of the first three bits in an index are used to pick\nan axis value from either the min or max vector of the AABB.\n0 = min, 1 = max.\nThis algorithm produces the following index scheme, where\nthe vertex at 0 is the \"min\" vertex and 7 is the \"max\":\n6---------7\n/|        /|\n/ |       / |\n4---------5  |\n|  |      |  |\n|  2------|--3\n| /       | /\n|/        |/\n0---------1"
    },
    {
      "id": "get-index",
      "name": "GetIndex",
      "category": "AABB",
      "signature": "GetIndex(Target, Axis Selector)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TAABB*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Axis Selector",
          "type": "FIntVector&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Int",
      "docs": "Given a point on a unit cube expressed as an IntVector of 0s and 1s, get the vertex index of that point.\n0 represents a negative axis and 1 represents a positive axis. All other values are invalid, but we do\nnot check this as it would add overhead to support functions. This is used by the support functions and\nmust invert the index logic in GetVertex()."
    },
    {
      "id": "get-edge",
      "name": "GetEdge",
      "category": "AABB",
      "signature": "GetEdge(Target, Index)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TAABB*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Index",
          "type": "Int"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "FAABBEdge",
      "docs": "Get an array of two indices into the vertex list for one of the\ntwelve edges of the box. Edges are ordered by increasing vertex\nindices.\nThis algorithm produces the following index scheme, where the\nbottom left vertex is the \"min\" vertex and the top right is \"max\":\n6-----11------7\n/|            /|\n9 |          10 |\n/  6          /  7\n4------8------5   |\n|   |         |   |\n|   2------5--|---3\n2  /          4  /\n| 1           | 3\n|/            |/\n0------0------1"
    },
